<title>MEXICO: Santander Investment director Avila resigns.</title>
<headline>Santander Investment director Avila resigns.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santander Investment Managing Director Joaquin Avila has resigned from the Madrid-based financial company, he said in a release.</p>
<p>Avila opened Santander Investment's Mexico City office in 1989.</p>
<p>Before resigning he was in charge of Santander's global capital market activities and head of their New York operations. He was also CEO of Santander Financial Products.</p>
<p>The release did not say why he was resigning.</p>
<p>Santander Investment is a subsidiary of Spain's Banco Santander SA.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
